          "distinct": true,
          "id": "3c81bb29ec87d282bc18b1701fadaaf8993dc114",
          "message": "DOCS: shim breathe crash on anonymous Doxygen sections\n\nDoxygen >= 1.9.7 wraps markdown headings that skip levels (a ### with no\nenclosing #/##) in anonymous, title-less <sect1>/<sect2> elements.\nBreathe's generated parser never sets .title on docSect2Type when the\nelement has no <title> child, so visit_docsectN crashes with\nAttributeError during sphinx-build. Latest breathe (4.36.0) is affected.\n\nPatch the renderer in conf.py to hoist the children of anonymous\nsections instead of emitting a section node — the same flat structure\nolder Doxygen produced. Also repoint the SphinxRenderer.methods dispatch\nentries, which captured the original function at class-definition time.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-15T11:14:22+02:00",
          "tree_id": "9b65bde08473655ca5ca5c886e7a9f06af6b9f10",
